301, 63%, 40%)">double</span><span class="token punctuation" style="color:hsl(119, 34%, 47%)">)</span><span class="token plain"> resp</span><span class="token operator" style="color:hsl(221, 87%, 60%)">-></span><span class="token plain">PauseRemaining </span><span class="token operator" style="color:hsl(221, 87%, 60%)">/</span><span class="token plain"> </span><span class="token number" style="color:hsl(35, 99%, 36%)">1E9</span><span class="token punctuation" style="color:hsl(119, 34%, 47%)">)</span><span class="token punctuation" style="color:hsl(119, 34%, 47%)">;</span><span class="token plain"></span><br/></div><div class=token-line style="color:hsl(230, 8%, 24%)"><span class="token plain">    </span><span class="token function" style="color:hsl(221, 87%, 60%)">jsConsumerPauseResponse_Destroy</span><span class="token punctuation" style="color:hsl(119, 34%, 47%)">(</span><span class="token plain">resp</span><span class="token punctuation" style="color:hsl(119, 34%, 47%)">)</span><span class="token punctuation" style="color:hsl(119, 34%, 47%)">;</span><span class="token plain"></span><br/></div><div class=token-line style="color:hsl(230, 8%, 24%)"><span class="token plain"></span><span class="token punctuation" style="color:hsl(119, 34%, 47%)">}</span><br/></div></code></pre></div></div></div></div></div>
<p><strong>Pausing does not stop publishers.</strong> Pause is a consumer setting, so it
doesn't change the stream. New messages keep arriving while the
<code>shipping</code> consumer is paused, and they count toward the stream's storage
limits. A long pause on a stream with a tight <code>MaxMsgs</code> or <code>MaxBytes</code> can
drop the oldest orders before the consumer reads them. Size the stream
for the longest pause you expect, or keep pauses short. See <a class="" href=/learn/jetstream/shaping-the-stream>Shaping
the stream</a> for how the limits
apply.</p>
<h2 class="anchor anchorTargetStickyNavbar_Vzrq" id=where-you-are>Where you are<a href=#where-you-are class=hash-link aria-label="Direct link to Where you are" title="Direct link to Where you are" translate=no>​</a></h2>
<p>The <code>shipping</code> consumer has been paused until a deadline and then
resumed. Its cursor stayed where it was: no messages were lost and none
were delivered twice by mistake.</p>
<p>The stream is unchanged, and the consumer is running again at the same
place it held before the pause.</p>
<h2 class="anchor anchorTargetStickyNavbar_Vzrq" id=whats-next>What's next<a href=#whats-next class=hash-link aria-label="Direct link to What's next" title="Direct link to What's next" translate=no>​</a></h2>
<p>With consumers covered, the next page returns to the stream itself: the
<a class="" href=/learn/jetstream/shaping-the-stream>limits and discard policy</a> that decide
what <code>ORDERS</code> keeps and what it drops once it fills up.</p>
<h2 class="anchor anchorTargetStickyNavbar_Vzrq" id=see-also>See also<a href=#see-also class=hash-link aria-label="Direct link to See also" title="Direct link to See also" translate=no>​</a></h2>
<ul>
<li class=""><a class="" href=/reference/jetstream/api/consumer/pause>Reference → Pause consumer</a> — the
<code>PauseUntil</code> field and the pause response.</li>
<li class=""><a class="" href=/reference/jetstream/advisory/consumer-pause>Reference → Consumer pause advisory</a>
— the notification the server sends when a consumer pauses or resumes.</li>
<li class=""><a class="" href=/learn/jetstream/pull-consumers>Pull consumers in depth</a> — the
consumer state that pausing preserves.</li>
